## Actions, in order

**1. Unblock the executor and open ballot B8 (two foreground Bash calls, parallel, each returns in seconds)**

```
herdr agent prompt wgka "Step 6 decision is on ballot B8 with the two advisors; result in ~25 min. Don't wait idle. Using superpowers:test-driven-development, implement step 6 with the source allow-list as ONE variable (no literal CIDRs elsewhere), provisional value 10.77.1.128/25 — provisional, not decided. Then continue every remaining plan step that doesn't depend on the value. Commit in the worktree only, marked 'provisional pending B8'. Do not request review or merge until I send you the B8 result." --wait --until working --timeout 30000
```

```
herdr agent prompt adv-fable "BALLOT B8 (read-only, vote independently). Worktree ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive, branch feat/wg-keepalive-relay, plan step 6: source allow-list for the WireGuard keepalive relay. Option 1: WireGuard /25 only, 10.77.1.128/25. Option 2: whole VPN /24, 10.77.1.0/24 (matches the front-door allow-list, also admits OpenVPN clients). Executor's claim to verify, not trust: only WireGuard clients send these keepalives. Reply exactly: 'B8 VOTE: 1|2', 'REASON: <=3 lines', 'RISKS: anything that would break the ccs-it canary'. Modify nothing." --wait --until working --timeout 30000
```

**2. Event-driven waits (two background Bash calls, `run_in_background: true`)**

```
herdr agent wait adv-fable --timeout 900000
herdr agent wait adv-codex --timeout 1200000
```

When the adv-codex wait fires, I read B7, then send it the identical B8 text and start a new background wait. I do not interrupt B7.

**3. Agent tool (Sonnet, background)**

The subagent updates `orchestrator/backlog.md` (wgka step 6 provisional, B8 open, "canary acceptance: waiting on operator, do not wake"), runs `build-backlog.sh`, and drafts the acceptance note. I then update the Artifact.

**4. On the B8 result**

- **2/2:** `herdr agent prompt wgka "B8: 2/2 for Option <n>. Value is final. Proceed to superpowers:verification-before-completion, then report for Codex cross-review."`
- **Split:** the question joins the morning poll; nothing merges on it.

**5. Acceptance**

Nothing goes to the operator now. After the canary is deployed from merged `main` and server-side checks are recorded in `soul/ccs-it.md`, my last action of the night is one AskUserQuestion:

> **Canary accept.** wg-keepalive canary is live on ccs-it (main @ `<sha>`). Acceptance needs you: connect with your own WireGuard profile and run `ping -i 0.2 172.27.96.2` for 3 minutes. Result?
> - Passed — no loss, no stalls
> - Failed — loss or stalls
> - Not tested yet — hold on ccs-it

## Why

The standing rule says I decide nothing myself. Agreeing with Option 1, last night's precedent and the time pressure don't change that. The ballot costs about 25 minutes, and the executor loses none of them: the allow-list is one variable, so the provisional value is a one-line change and nothing merges before the vote.

adv-fable is idle, so it starts now. adv-codex finishes B7 undisturbed, because interrupting a review would damage a second decision. Neither advisor sees my opinion or the executor's recommendation, so the votes stay independent.

Background waits keep my session free to handle other tabs.

The acceptance needs the operator's own profile. I can't substitute another peer and call it accepted, and a 3-minute ping isn't worth waking them for. "Canary on ccs-it tonight" is satisfied by deploying it. It stays on ccs-it only, with the poll waiting when they wake. The poll goes last because it blocks my session.
